{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"The root cause was the `recommendation` Service, and I fixed it and submitted the mitigation. After the fix, `/api/recommendations` returned 200 in about 12 ms in three straight checks, where before it timed out.\n\n- **Cause:** the `recommendation` Service had `internalTrafficPolicy: Local`. The `recommendation` pod is pinned to `kind-worker` and the `frontend` pod to `kind-worker2`. With that policy, `frontend` couldn't reach the Service's ClusterIP, and recommendation requests timed out.\n- **Fix:** I patched the Service to `internalTrafficPolicy: Cluster`.\n- **Frontend restart:** the `frontend` gRPC client was still failing against the cached connection error, so I restarted the `frontend` deployment.\n- **Not changed:** the `otel-collector` Service also uses `Local`. I left it because it runs as a per-node DaemonSet, so that setting is normal.\n- **Submission:** I sent the empty-solution POST to the submit endpoint once, and it returned \"Submission received\".\n\nI didn't check latency on other endpoints after the fix."}}
